# A lens whose focus is a library's type: `put` writes a Fraction into the file and `get` gives it back inside an
# Entry. Building the Fraction in `get` is a call into the library, no occurrence: it is glued into `Entry(..)`, which
# is handed the ledger whose path it reads. `put`'s Fraction is its parameter `amount`, a value from beyond.

route books.ledger.Ledger
step Ledger()/Ledger()
step Ledger()/Ledger.put
step Ledger()/Ledger.get
step Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry()

line entry > Ledger()/Ledger() call
line entry > Ledger()/Ledger.put call
line entry > Ledger()/Ledger.get call
line Ledger()/Ledger() > Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger() value
line Ledger > Ledger()/Ledger.put value # the caller's instance: every method runs on it
line Fraction·amount > Ledger()/Ledger.put value
line Ledger > Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() value # `Entry(Fraction(self.path.read_text()))` hands the ledger
line Ledger()/Ledger.put > Disk(Ledger.path) own
line Disk(Ledger.path) > Ledger()/Ledger.get own
line Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() > Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() value
line Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() > Ledger()/Ledger.get value
line Ledger()/Ledger.get > Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get value

home Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger() Ledger()
home Ledger Ledger()
home Fraction·amount Ledger()
home Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() Ledger()/Ledger.get
home Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get Ledger()

side entry left
side Disk(Ledger.path) between
# what the constructor builds goes back to its caller: Atlas runs the methods on it instead of the caller's instance
